---
/**
 * Cookie policy: the English counterpart of `src/pages/cookie-policy.astro`.
 *
 * A separate route rather than a section of the privacy policy: ePrivacy requires
 * the description of cookies to be reachable BEFORE consent is given, that is,
 * from the banner itself.
 *
 * Same facts, same structure and the same effective date as the Bulgarian page:
 * exactly the records this site really sets. Empty categories are listed as
 * empty rather than left out.
 *
 * The Bulgarian page is the legally binding one; the first paragraph says so.
 */
import Text from '../../layouts/Text.astro';
import { crumbSchema, bizRef } from '../../lib/seo';
import { BUSINESS as b } from '../../config/site';
import { LEGAL_EN, ROUTES } from '../../i18n';
import { dict } from '../../i18n/ui';

const path = '/en/cookies/';
const bgPath = ROUTES.find((r) => r.en === path)!.bg;
const [privacy, terms] = LEGAL_EN;
const t = dict('en');

const updated = '8 September 2026';
const address = `${b.address.streetEn}, ${b.address.cityEn} ${b.address.postalCode}`;

const site = Astro.site!.href.replace(/\/$/, '');
const schema = [
  bizRef(site, 'en'),
  crumbSchema(site, [{ href: '/en/', label: 'Home' }, { href: path, label: 'Cookie policy' }]),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    url: `${site}${path}`,
    name: 'Cookie policy',
    description: 'Which cookies PDK Tuning uses, in which categories, for how long and how to decline them.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: '2026-09-08',
    about: { '@id': `${site}/#business` },
  },
];
---
<Text
  title="Cookie policy — PDK Tuning"
  description="Which cookies the PDK Tuning site uses, by category and duration, which providers set them and how to withdraw your consent at any time."
  heading="Cookie policy"
  lead={`The site works entirely without tracking cookies. Nothing that tracks is loaded before you press “${t.ccYes}”; it is not loaded first and switched off afterwards.`}
  updated={updated}
  schema={schema}
>
  <p class="doc-binding">
    This English text is provided for convenience and has not been reviewed by a lawyer;
    the legally binding version is the <a href={bgPath} hreflang="bg">Bulgarian original</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What a cookie is</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small record that a site leaves in your browser so that it can remember
    something the next time the page loads. Besides cookies proper, the browser has another
    kind of storage, <strong>localStorage</strong>. In law the two are treated the same, and they
    are described together here, because for you the difference does not matter.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The four categories</h2>
  <p>
    The split follows the practice of the supervisory authorities. For each category we say
    whether this site actually uses it, including when the answer is no.
  </p>

  <h3>2.1. Strictly necessary: always active</h3>
  <p>
    Without them the site cannot carry out an action you have explicitly asked for. No consent
    is requested for them, because without them there is no service. They cannot be switched
    off from the banner.
  </p>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Set by</th><th>What for</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td data-l="Record"><code>pdk-consent</code><br /><em>localStorage</em></td>
        <td data-l="Set by">this site</td>
        <td data-l="What for">remembers your cookie choice so that we do not ask on every page load</td>
        <td data-l="Duration">up to 12 months</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td data-l="Record"><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
        <td data-l="Set by">Cloudflare</td>
        <td data-l="What for">tells a person from an automated client; protects the form from abuse</td>
        <td data-l="Duration">30 minutes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td data-l="Record"><code>cf_clearance</code></td>
        <td data-l="Set by">Cloudflare</td>
        <td data-l="What for">set only if the protection has asked you to pass a check; remembers that you passed it</td>
        <td data-l="Duration">up to 30 days</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>2.2. Functional: not used</h3>
  <p>
    The site does not remember language, font, display preferences or anything else between
    visits. This category is <strong>empty</strong>, which is why it does not appear in the
    banner.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3. Statistics: only with consent</h3>
  <p>
    The only category we ask you about. It tells us how many people come and which pages they
    read, not who you are.
  </p>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Set by</th><th>What for</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td data-l="Record"><code>_ga</code></td>
        <td data-l="Set by">Google Analytics 4</td>
        <td data-l="What for">tells one device from another, so that one person is not counted ten times</td>
        <td data-l="Duration">up to 24 months</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td data-l="Record"><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td>
        <td data-l="Set by">Google Analytics 4</td>
        <td data-l="What for">keeps the state of the visit</td>
        <td data-l="Duration">up to 24 months</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <strong>How exactly it is held back until you say yes:</strong> Google's script is not in
    the page. It is not downloaded, not run, and not "loaded but not counting". The code that
    adds it runs only after you press the button. If you decline, or withdraw consent you gave
    earlier, the tag is switched off and any <code>_ga*</code> records already set are deleted.
  </p>
  <p>
    The IP address sent to Google is anonymised. Your choice is also passed on through Google
    Consent Mode, with the advertising permissions explicitly set to <em>denied</em>.
  </p>

  <h3>2.4. Marketing: not used</h3>
  <p>
    There are <strong>no</strong> advertising pixels on this site: no Meta Pixel, no TikTok, no
    LinkedIn, no Google Ads remarketing. We do not build advertising profiles and do not share
    data for cross-site targeted advertising. The category is empty and there is nothing to
    decline.
  </p>

  <h2>3. The partner portal</h2>
  <p>
    The login for partner workshops runs on a separate system on our older server. When you
    sign in there, it sets a session cookie (<code>PHPSESSID</code>) that keeps you signed in.
    It is strictly necessary for the login and is deleted when you close the browser. If you do
    not use the portal, this cookie never appears.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How to change your decision</h2>
  <p>
    At any time, press <strong>{t.cookieSettings}</strong> at the bottom of any page. The banner
    opens again and you can change your choice in either direction. If you decline, statistics
    records already set are deleted straight away.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also delete and block cookies in the browser itself, under
    <em>Settings → Privacy</em>. Bear in mind that blocking cookies completely affects many
    sites, not just this one.
  </p>

  <h2>5. If you do not accept</h2>
  <p>
    The site works fully. There is no restricted content, no repeating banner and no wall. The
    only difference is that we will not count you in the statistics.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The controller is <strong>{b.legalName}</strong>, trading as {b.name}, {address}.
    Questions and requests: <a href={`mailto:${b.email}`}>{b.email}</a>,
    <a href={`tel:${b.phone}`}>{b.phoneIntl}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    How we process personal data in general is set out in the
    <a href={privacy.href}>privacy policy</a>. The terms for using the site and the services
    are in the <a href={terms.href}>terms and conditions</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we add a new provider or a new category, we update this page, change the date at the top
    and <strong>ask for your consent again</strong>. Consent you gave earlier does not cover
    something that was not described when you gave it.
  </p>
</Text>

<style is:global>
/* The binding-version note opens the body. */
.doc-body .doc-binding{color:var(--ink-3);font-style:italic}
</style>
